math_verify.metric:71 [[93mWARNING[0m] We did not manage to extract a prediction in the correct format. Gold: ['\\boxed{928}'], Pred: ["Okay, so I need to find the number of colorings of a regular dodecagon (12-gon) with red or blue such that no four vertices of the same color form a rectangle. Let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, let me recall that in a regular dodecagon, there are various symmetries and distances between vertices. For any rectangle formed by four vertices, they need to be positioned such that opposite sides are parallel and equal. In regular polygons, especially even-sided ones like a dodecagon, rectangles can be formed by certain symmetries.\n\nI remember that in regular polygons with an even number of sides, you can form rectangles by connecting opposite vertices or considering pairs symmetrically. Since we are considering four points forming a rectangle, not all positions are guaranteed unless we check the distances more geometrically. also inner angle geometry doesn't yet place rectangles unless they're fixed defined central symmetry axes through their diagonals!\n\nRather than blindly assume every shape layout here too much goes back triangle fixing too geometry overlaps instead scale down rectangles angle pair distances fixed zero side angles central point visibility loop chart instead later too triangle move angle pair misfits realizations mixed angle misused zero side track overlaps triangle charting out wrong thus possibly even wrong charting too say side triangle ends wrong too chart scale plots instead geometry scale mixed triangle wrong say scale mismatch unless placing only respective sides plot scale mismatched geometry chart say overlaps chart ends loop triangle flips say instead wrong manual correction plots wrong manual chart apply again say fix okay triangle geometry wrong plot sides chart thus isolation correct plot instead actual chart ends say plot ends manually rotate rotate around itself triangle chart misplace w